Tracing: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines distributed tracing policy, trace structure, and
  code-to-trace mapping rules.

TraceStructure:
  TraceID:
    - Unique per request
    - Propagated across all services

  SpanID:
    - Unique per operation
    - Parent-child relationship

  Context:
    - service
    - operation
    - start_time
    - end_time
    - duration
    - status
    - tags (key-value pairs)
    - logs (timestamped events within span)

Propagation:
  - HTTP: X-Trace-ID header
  - gRPC: metadata propagation
  - Message queues: message headers

Sampling:
  Development: 100%
  Production: 1-10% (configurable)
  Errors: 100% for error traces

CodeTraceMapping:
  trace:
    <operation.name>
  ↓
  service:
    ./<layer>/<domain>/<module>/<artifact>
  ↓
  component:
    <ComponentName>
  ↓
  task:
    <TASK-ID>

LatencyAnalysis:
  - Identify slow spans
  - Compare against baseline
  - Detect regressions

CrossLayer:
  Architecture: Service dependency mapping
  Diagnostics: Trace analysis for root cause
  Incident: Trace correlation for impact analysis

State: +
  